From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:47:52 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: glymur-hp-omnibook-ultra-kg0xxx: poll for
 SCMI completions

With the CPUCP mailbox built as a module, the SCMI performance protocol
times out at boot (-110) and cpufreq never comes up. Built in, it
avoids the timeout but the board resets silently minutes after boot.

Set arm,no-completion-irq so the SCMI transport polls for completions
instead of waiting for the mailbox interrupt. Why the completions go
missing is not known. A glymur-wide version was proposed in [1]; drop
this once the cause is fixed.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260808172211.137577-1-jesse.casco@gmail.com [1]
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/glymur-hp-omnibook-ultra-kg0xxx.dts     | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-hp-omnibook-ultra-kg0xxx.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-hp-omnibook-ultra-kg0xxx.dts
index 1c5b6859079a..fec7c87d36f3 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-hp-omnibook-ultra-kg0xxx.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-hp-omnibook-ultra-kg0xxx.dts
@@ -669,6 +669,14 @@ nvme_reg_en: nvme-reg-en-state {
 	};
 };
 
+/*
+ * Without polling, SCMI needs the CPUCP mailbox interrupt at boot
+ * (CONFIG_QCOM_CPUCP_MBOX=y), which resets this board at random.
+ */
+&{/firmware/scmi} {
+	arm,no-completion-irq;
+};
+
 &pmk8850_rtc {
 	qcom,no-alarm;
 };
